  "notes": "An AI study companion for lecture PDFs. Warm off-white chrome (#f6f5f2) surrounds white panels with 12px radii. The defining detail is the inline visualization chips: 96x18 pills (999px radius, 1px tinted border, small shadow), each with a type icon and truncated label. Each visualization type has its own pastel colour: pink for 3D Model, lavender for Formula, blue for Graph, amber for Animation and green for Source. Clicking a chip switches the right panel to a 'Visualizer' mode with an interactive WebGL 3D model and a caption. The right panel's mode dropdown also offers Knowledge Graph, Flashcards, Quizzes and Feynman modes. User chat bubbles are near-black (#111113) with white text; AI replies are on warm grey (#f3f2ef). A floating pill toolbar at the bottom of the document holds paging and zoom controls. The Settings icon opens a popover (Model Engine, model selects, Light/System/Dark segmented control, Auto-generate toggle); it is not open in the capture. I filed a new-entry proposal, inline-entity-chip, for the viz chips."
